🗣️ Communication Practice — 100–200 Words

Topic: My Approach to Learning New Technology

When I learn a new technology, I first understand the problem it is designed to solve. Instead of memorizing commands, I try to understand the basic concept and architecture. Then I build a small example so that I can see how the technology works in practice. After understanding the fundamentals, I explore more advanced features and common problems. I also compare the technology with alternatives because understanding the differences helps me choose the right tool for a particular situation. Finally, I explain what I learned in my own words. If I cannot explain something simply, I know that I need to study it again. This approach helps me remember concepts for a longer time and also prepares me to answer technical questions during interviews.

🎤 Speaking task:

Explain one technology you know using:

What it is → Why it is used → How it works → Example.


